    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter tonight\u2019s slate with **Yordan Alvarez** providing the clear anchor for the lineup; his score of 87.42 is fueled by an elite xwOBA of .474 and a prime matchup against Grayson Rodriguez (5.28 xERA), making him the must-start asset of the day. We are also leaning heavily into our speed-focused strategy, prioritizing **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (69.53) and **Caleb Durbin** (72.37). Both benefit from high-upside matchups against pitchers with slow deliveries, creating a prime environment for stolen bases\u2014our scarcest category. **Dillon Dingler** (63.75) remains a standout start behind the dish, as his 12% boost from the opposing pitcher\u2019s skill profile and favorable dynamic platoon edge make him a significantly stronger play than **Gary Sanchez** (46.47), who struggles against the durability of Logan Webb.\n\nWe remain cautious regarding **Carson Benge** (57.57), whose projection is tempered by a 45% rain risk in his contest against Smith-Shawver; while his matchup is statistically favorable, the weather introduces a volatility we are monitoring closely. On the bench, **Pedro Ramirez** (39.68) was the closest candidate for a call-up, ultimately falling short due to his projected #9 batting order position which suppresses his run-scoring ceiling. Meanwhile, **Lars Nootbaar** (43.22) makes the lineup despite a lukewarm score, as we prioritize his availability over **Chase Meidroth** (34.97), whose matchup against a sub-3.00 xERA arm like Cam Schlittler effectively neutralized his utility today. We are keeping **Hyeseong Kim** and **Kyle Schwarber** sidelined as they remain inactive, focusing our daily game caps on the active core of **Trea Turner**, **Kazuma Okamoto**, **Junior Caminero**, **Nelson Velazquez**, **Christian Yelich**, **Josh Smith**, and the aforementioned starters.",
